 "title": "Geographic (re)naming proposals",
 "hook": "When someone wants to officially name or rename a geographic feature of the United States — such as a mountain, creek, or island — they file a proposal with the US Board on Geographic Names. Those proposals end up on the agency’s “Action List,” the most recent year of which can be downloaded as a spreadsheet.",
